* >Natural Source Header 000000
* :Mode S
* :CP
* :LineIncrement 10
* <Natural Source Header
*
* Member     : RMBUNSEQ
*
* Purpose    : Exit for determining sequence of reports in a bundle
*
* Description: This is a very special purpose exit which will normally
*              be distributed only in object format. By special request
*              the source is delivered to a customer for them to tailor.
*
*              RMBUNSEQ is passed a bundle name and run number, from
*              which it must deduce whether the bundle is to be printed
*              in the old sequence (ISN, more or less report arrival
*              sequence) used by NOM135 or in the new sequence
*              introduced by solution OM135A7 (report name/run number
*              sequence).
*              The print sequence is governed by the setting of the
*              third parameter:
*
*              TRUE  - the new sequence is used
*              FALSE - the old sequence is used
*
* Author     : SJU
* Date       : 02.02.2001
*
* Maintenance
* uuu     yyyy-mm-dd s(999999) ...
* sju     2001-02-02 p(193780) created
* xsetggr 2007-05-03 NOM3201   support 11 byte run numbers
* fhi     2008-06-24 P306370   recataloged, not reproducible error
* --------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFINE DATA PARAMETER
1 P-BUNDLE-NAME  (A25) /* Input bundle name - do not change
1 P-BUNDLE-RNB   (P11) /* Input bundle run number - do not change
* xsetggr 2007-05-03  NOM3201 change line above from P7
1 P-NEW-SEQUENCE (L)   /* Output - set to TRUE or FALSE
END-DEFINE
P-NEW-SEQUENCE:= TRUE                  /* Use new sequence by default
*
* Insert logic here to check bundle name in case it must be printed
* using the old sequence, for example:
* IF P-BUNDLE-NAME = 'UKSJUBUN'
*   P-NEW-SEQUENCE:= FALSE
* END-IF
*
END
